.TH STAR-SEARCH 1 "September 2026" "star-search 0.1.0"
.SH NAME
star-search \- query an offline stellar catalog
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B star-search
.RB [ --json ]
.B info
.I NAME_OR_ID
.br
.B star-search
.RB [ --json ]
.B star
.I NAME_OR_ID
.br
.B star-search
.RB [ --json ]
.B coords
.I NAME_OR_ID
.br
.B star-search
.RB [ --json ]
.B nearest
.I N
.br
.B star-search
.RB [ --json ]
.B recons-nearest
.RI [ N ]
.br
.B star-search
.RB [ --json ]
.B recons-info
.I NAME_OR_ID
.br
.B star-search
.RB [ --json ]
.B render
.I NAME_OR_ID
.br
.B star-search
.RB [ --json ]
.RB [ --catalog-info | --version ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Queries local Parquet data through embedded DuckDB. With no command, prompts
for one star name or stable ID. No network lookup or extension download occurs.
Exact stable IDs take precedence over exact names and aliases, followed by
literal substring search. Ambiguity produces up to ten candidates ordered by ID.
Select a component by performing another lookup with its stable ID.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B info
Show identity, distance, coordinates, epoch, and available photometry.
Unknown fields print as unknown, or null in JSON.
.TP
.B star
Alias of
.BR info .
.TP
.B coords
Show ICRS and Galactic coordinates in degrees and the reference epoch.
Coordinates are not propagated to the current date.
.TP
.B nearest N
Show the nearest N catalog entries with known positive distances from the Sun.
N must be between 1 and 10000. Ties are ordered by stable ID.
.TP
.B recons-nearest [N]
Show RECONS stellar components in the first N ranked systems, default 100.
N must be between 1 and 100. This is the RECONS list accurate as of 2012-01-01,
not a current census. RECONS data must be available beside the catalog or through
.BR STAR_SEARCH_RECONS_DATA .
.TP
.B recons-info NAME_OR_ID
Look up a RECONS CNS name, common name, or component ID. Ambiguous systems require
selecting one of the displayed stable IDs.
.TP
.B render NAME_OR_ID
Reserved for the deterministic star portrait renderer. Not yet implemented:
prints a diagnostic, writes no file, and exits with status 5.
.TP
.B --catalog-info
Show source release, selection policy, attribution, and limitations.
.TP
.B --json
Emit an object for a single lookup or an array for nearest.
IDs are strings. Distances are in parsecs. Errors are JSON objects.
Prompts and diagnostics go to stderr.
.TP
.B --version
Show the program version without opening a catalog.
.TP
.B --help
Show command syntax without opening a catalog.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B STAR_SEARCH_DATA_DIR
Override the catalog directory, normally /usr/share/star-search.
It must contain stars.parquet, aliases.parquet, and catalog.json.
Paths containing glob characters are not supported.
.TP
.B STAR_SEARCH_RECONS_DATA
Optional path to recons_nearest.parquet. If unset, star-search checks the catalog
directory for that file.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 success; 1 runtime or catalog error; 2 invalid usage; 3 no match;
4 ambiguous match; 5 not implemented (render).
.SH LIMITATIONS
The development fixture is synthetic and not suitable for scientific use.
Nearest results describe the installed catalog, not a complete census.
There is no online enrichment, mass estimation, or luminosity estimation.
The RECONS source list is a 2012 snapshot and uses measurements from mixed
references. Catalogs built from the merged RECONS x Gaia DR3 data record the
cross-match provenance per row; see docs/data-schemas.md.